r own most of the  time especially once you get into the  higher ranks carrying a game becomes  harder and harder to a point of  eventually it might become impossible  and you'll need to use your teammates to  get an edge on the match think of each  play as a possession if your team has  the ball more than the other team your  chances of winning the game  skyrocket if the other team can't get  the ball  they can't score on you it's very simple  and it makes a lot of sense but it's  something most players don't really  think of ever in your upcoming matches  focus on the amount of time you and your  teammates have possession of the ball  and if you don't have the ball think  about how you can get it back into your  possession you'll likely find that this  leads to better play from you and leads  to better results with solo queue  teammates  the final piece of advice that i have  for you guys and this is a big one is to  ignore the haters  ignore the toxicity you're 100 percent  going to have to endure when solo  queuing rocky this game is extremely  competitive and when you mix  competitiveness with the anonymity of  the internet and most likely younger  gamers you're going to get toxicity  rampant toxicity so just remember that  no one can judge your own gameplay if  someone thinks you're bad ignore it if  someone thinks you're slow ignore it  someone thinks you're a ball chaser  ignore that too if they want you to play  a certain way just ignore it more likely  than not they're projecting their own  problems onto other players and honestly  it's just super cringe you don't need to  respond and it doesn't even deserve a  response if you're doing your best and  working hard on what you need to work on  as a player then nothing else really  matters you're the only judge of your  own ability and the only people you need  to listen to is your coach the people  who support you and most importantly  yourself so i'd recommend just turning  off game chat entirely most of th